    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The originalist interpretation of the Second Amendment, which holds that the right to keep and bear arms is an individual right unconnected to militia service, is the only correct reading of the Constitution and was affirmed by the Supreme Court in *District of Columbia v. Heller*. In contrast, the living constitutionalist approach, which argues that gun rights must be balanced against public safety concerns and can be limited by modern judicial discretion, is a dangerous distortion that undermines the Founders' intent to secure liberty. The originalist view is the only one that truly respects the text and history of the Bill of Rights, while the living constitutionalist method is a slippery slope toward judicial overreach that erodes fundamental freedoms.",
